CON-15: KINWAVE: raise the inlet area only by what the inflow fills

KWSolver::solveConduit() copies legacy's no-flow branch: when the rise in
inlet area needs more water than the step supplies, f(a) > 0 on the whole
bracket, the outlet area is clamped to 0 and the conduit is booked with
water that never entered. In that branch, lower the inlet area to the value
for which the equation holds with aout = 0 (C2 = 0), never below the
previous inlet area, as the 5.3.0 patch does.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-15_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydraulics/KinematicWave.cpp b/src/engine/hydraulics/KinematicWave.cpp
index a79bd76..25c65c5 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydraulics/KinematicWave.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydraulics/KinematicWave.cpp
@@ -337,6 +337,11 @@ int KWSolver::solveConduit(int idx, const XSectParams& xs,
         // both bounds positive → no flow
         a = 0.0;
         result = -3;
+        // CON-15: the inflow cannot fill the rise in inlet area within this
+        // step; raise the inlet area only by what it fills, so that
+        // continuity still holds
+        if (a_in_norm > prev_a1)
+            a_in_norm = std::max(prev_a1, a_in_norm - C2 * WX / ((1.0 - WT) * dxdt));
     } else {
         result = -1;
     }
